  "claim": "An area is delimited by a 3.5 mi long tributary containing an estimated 30000000 USgal of spilled oil. The neighbourhood of Williamsburg, Brooklyn is in this area.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Brooklyn Community Board 1. Sentence: Brooklyn Community Board 1 is a New York City community board that encompasses the Brooklyn neighborhoods of Williamsburg and Greenpoint.\nPage: Brooklyn Community Board 1. Sentence: It is delimited by the Newtown Creek and Queens Borough line on the east, Flushing and Kent Avenue on the south, and by the East River on the west.\nPage: Newtown Creek. Sentence: Newtown Creek, a 3.5 mi long tributary of the East River, is an estuary that forms part of the border between the boroughs of Brooklyn and Queens, in New York City.\nPage: Newtown Creek. Sentence: Channelization made it one of the most heavily used bodies of water in the Port of New York and New Jersey and thus one of the most polluted industrial sites in the US, containing years of discarded toxins, an estimated 30000000 USgal of spilled oil, including the Greenpoint oil spill, raw sewage from New York City’s sewer system, and other accumulation from a total of 1,491 sites.\nPage: Williamsburg, Brooklyn. Sentence: Part of Brooklyn Community Board 1, the neighborhood is served in the south by the NYPD's 90th Precinct and in the north by the 94th Precinct.",
